    "raw": "Given:\n- Tommy's home is now worth 25% more than what he bought it for.\n- He sells this home and buys a new one for $500,000.\n- He takes a loan for 75% of the new house's cost, meaning he pays 25% of the new house's cost.\n\nLet's denote the price Tommy bought his first house for as \\( x \\).\n\nSince the home is now worth 25% more than what he bought it for, the current value of the home is \\( 1.25x \\).\n\nHe sells this home and uses the proceeds to buy a new house for $500,000. He pays 25% of the new house's cost, which means he pays \\( 0.25 \\times 500,000 = 125,000 \\).\n\nSo, the equation for the sale price of his first home is:\n\\[ 1.25x = 125,000 \\]\n\nTo find \\( x \\), we solve the equation:\n\\[ x = \\frac{125,000}{1.25} \\]\n\\[ x = 100,000 \\]\n\nSo, Tommy bought his first house for $100,000.\n\nFINAL: 100000",
